<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!--
        Every build that is not a release paints the mark yellow.

        Shared by the debug and releaseTest source sets rather than living in
        either of them. A minified build handed over for testing is exactly as
        much "not the real app" as a debug one, and the first one that went out
        was indistinguishable from the release install on the launcher.

        Every place the bell appears follows from this one value: the launcher
        icon, the system splash, the widget header, and NightbellMark in the app
        itself, which reads the same resource. Deliberately not Amber #FFB020,
        which is the degraded status colour: a mark in the same shade as a
        warning would read as one.
    -->
    <color name="brand_mark">#FFFFD400</color>
</resources>
